{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>YHWH</b> — the sense of בקר is \"every morning,\" as in: חדשים לבקרים." "<b>And I will array [my prayer] to You</b> — it is deficient, as if it said אערוך לך תפלתי, as I explained. For the force of nouns extends to verbs: וברך and לא אשיבנה and ברוב יועצים תקום are in the futures as if written above כי אליך אתפלל תפלתי, and the word לך, with בקר אערוך לך, draws itself and another along with it, like יכפה אף והנה הוא, and אצפה לך."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {1 "The root citation לא אשיבנה does not correspond to any form in Psalm 5; possibly a corrupt or displaced reference, rendered hyper-literally as found."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:07.101516705Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}